The ZpPortal is an extension of the standard model  with a new vector boson
and a Dirac fermion as dark matter. It is assumed that the couplings the Z' mediator to all fermions is vectorial.
The file main.c can be used to compute the relic density in different cases according to
the definition chosen near the top of the file.

1- freeze-out:  uncomment #define OMEGA
2- freeze-in :  uncomment #define FREEZEIN

Two sample input files are provided for freeze-in (dataAll.par and datax.par).
More details can be found in
G. Bélanger, F. Boudjema, A. Goudelis, A. Pukhov, and B. Zaldivar,
"micrOMEGAs5.0 : Freeze-in," Comput. Phys. Commun. 231 (2018) 173,
arXiv:1801.03509 [hep-ph].

3- Entropy injection due to massive inflaton decays into SM radia-
tion :  uncomment #define INFLDECAY

Two sample input files are provided (infl1.par  and infl_fig5.par). Note that the model contains two additional parameters :
Gamma (total with of inflaton into SM particles) and H0 (the Hubble rate in the beginning of reheating), these parameters
are needed as input for the getInflDecay routine. The numerical values of these parameters can be specified in the input files.
As for all input parameters they can be extracted by the function findValW of micrOMEGAs, see main.c. 

For more details, see
G. Bélanger, N. Bernal and A. Pukhov
"Z'-mediated dark matter with low-temperature reheating"
arXiv:2412.12303 [hep-ph].
